{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target working && sed -n '1,260p' .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md && git diff -- src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc docs/design/dao.stream.md && nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc | sed -n '1,220p' && nl -ba test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc | sed -n '1,280p'\"","aggregated_output":"2026-09-10 12:58:11.242 xcodebuild[83646:21980036]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-09-10 12:58:11.550 xcodebuild[83646:21980035] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-SqaJmbvw' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-09-10 12:58:12.137 xcodebuild[83651:21980059]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-09-10 12:58:12.291 xcodebuild[83651:21980056] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n# Code Review Summary for `working`\n\n## Executive Overview\n- **Total Files Changed:** 3\n- **Lines Added:** +29 | **Lines Deleted:** -2\n- **Test-to-Source Additions Ratio:** 28.0 (28 test lines vs 1 source lines)\n- **Overall Change Risk:** `LOW`\n\n### Included Commits\n- 3102152 refactor(jing): move the remote content adapter to dao.stream\n- fa94413 docs(agents): reorganize team roster, cost constraints, and orchestrator role\n- aa232ab docs(agents): update model roster and document model strengths/weaknesses\n- f1babc8 test(stream): note that a real abort re-enters onError\n- f57bfff feat(jing): add the portable core dao.jing.remote's v2 client will turn\n\n## Automated Scan Findings\n✅ No critical security or code quality smells detected by automated scan.\n\n## File Churn & Risk Breakdown\n| File Path | Category | +Add | -Del | Risk |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc` | Source Code | +1 | -1 | `Medium` |\n| `test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc` | Tests | +28 | -0 | `Low` |\n| `docs/design/dao.stream.md` | Documentation | +0 | -1 | `Low` |\n\n## Reviewer Focus & Recommendations\n# Code Review PR Checklist & Taxonomy\n\nWhen performing code reviews, evaluate changes using this structured checklist and severity taxonomy.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Finding Severity Taxonomy\n\n| Severity | Label | Definition | Examples |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **P0** | **Critical (Blocker)** | Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, production crashes, secret leakage. Must be fixed before merging. | Hardcoded tokens, unhandled NullPointer on critical path, SQL injection, broken auth check. |\n| **P1** | **High (Must Address)** | Logic bugs, breaking API changes, missing error handling on external calls, race conditions, lack of tests for complex logic. | Swallowed exceptions, broken retry loop, missing backward compatibility in API schema. |\n| **P2** | **Medium (Recommended)** | Performance inefficiencies, code duplication, sub-optimal data structures, non-idiomatic style. | Unnecessary DB query inside loop, missing index, missing parameter validation. |\n| **P3** | **Low (Nit / Suggestion)** | Minor formatting, naming improvements, leftover comments/TODOs, minor doc polish. | Variable naming clarity, typos in docstrings, cleaning leftover TODO comments. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Comprehensive Review Checklist\n\n### A. Logic & Correctness\n- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Does the code handle null/nil/undefined, empty collections, zero values, boundary numbers, and unexpected inputs?\n- [ ] **State & Concurrency**: Are shared state mutations thread-safe? Are locks acquired/released properly without deadlock risks?\n- [ ] **Control Flow**: Are all conditional branches covered? Do loops have guaranteed termination conditions?\n- [ ] **Error Propagation**: Are errors caught and logged/surfaced appropriately, rather than swallowed silently (`catch (Exception e) {}`)?\n\n### B. Security & Credentials\n- [ ] **No Hardcoded Secrets**: Are API keys, passwords, bearer tokens, or private keys excluded from code and config?\n- [ ] **Input Validation & Sanitization**: Are external inputs validated before processing or passing to system shells, DB queries, or HTML rendering?\n- [ ] **Authentication & Authorization**: Do endpoints verify user identity and check permissions before executing state changes?\n- [ ] **Safe Dependencies**: Are newly added packages pinned to trusted versions without known vulnerabilities?\n\n### C. Architecture & API Design\n- [ ] **Preserve API Contracts**: Are public method signatures, REST endpoints, and schema definitions backward compatible?\n- [ ] **Single Responsibility**: Are modules, classes, and functions focused on a clear, single responsibility?\n- [ ] **Coupling & Cohesion**: Is the new code properly modularized without introducing circular dependencies or leaky abstractions?\n- [ ] **Idempotence**: Are retry loops or state-changing operations safe to re-execute on transient failures?\n\n### D. Performance & Resource Efficiency\n- [ ] **N+1 Queries**: Are database or remote API calls executed in batches rather than inside loops?\n- [ ] **Resource Cleanup**: Are file handles, database connections, streams, and web sockets closed explicitly (or managed via try-with-resources / context managers)?\n- [ ] **Memory & Allocation**: Are large datasets streamed or paginated rather than loaded fully into memory at once?\n\n### E. Test Coverage & Quality\n- [ ] **Test Coverage**: Do new features or bug fixes include corresponding unit or integration tests?\n- [ ] **Test Quality**: Do tests verify actual assertions rather than just checking that code runs without throwing?\n- [ ] **Edge Case Tests**: Are failure modes, invalid inputs, and error handlers covered by unit tests?\n\n---\n\n## 3. Review Feedback Guidelines\n\n1. **Be Specific**: Always reference the exact file line number, function name, and context.\n2. **Explain the \"Why\"**: Don't just say \"change this\". Explain the risk or benefit (e.g., \"This could lead to a race condition if two threads call `transact!` simultaneously...\").\n3. **Provide Concrete Fixes**: Offer concrete, copy-pasteable diff snippets where appropriate.\n4. **Acknowledge Good Work**: Highlight well-crafted solutions, thorough tests, or clean refactorings.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-F0ixGlsD' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-09-10 12:58:19.261 xcodebuild[83702:21980309]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-09-10 12:58:19.413 xcodebuild[83702:21980308] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-PcwqiiBY' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-09-10 12:58:19.904 xcodebuild[83706:21980326]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-09-10 12:58:20.067 xcodebuild[83706:21980325] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ndiff --git a/docs/design/dao.stream.md b/docs/design/dao.stream.md\nindex 9acbd3e..d8f6874 100644\n--- a/docs/design/dao.stream.md\n+++ b/docs/design/dao.stream.md\n@@ -801,7 +801,6 @@ completed; the decision it left open outlived it, and a transient plan is\n safe to delete only once nothing in it is still owed.\n \n The remaining v1 consumers, each migrating under its own plan:\n-`dao.jing`'s DHT node,\n `yin.io`'s file transports with `dao.gui.event` and\n `dao.postgraphics.terminal`, `dao.runtime` (gated on the v1 VM's deletion),\n `agent.tools`, and the demo and server surfaces. The v1 VM lineage is deleted\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc b/src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc\nindex e667cec..286f276 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc\n@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@\n                     [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n                     [dao.jing.dht :as dht]\n                     [dao.jing.dht.kad :as kad]\n-                    [dao.stream.transit :as transit]))\n+                    [dao.stream.transit :as transit]))\n   ;; :cljd nil must come FIRST: reader conditionals take the first\n   ;; matching branch, and the cljd host pass also matches :clj, so with\n   ;; :clj written first the import still reaches the Dart compiler.\ndiff --git a/test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc b/test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc\nindex fa7c285..03754c9 100644\n--- a/test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc\n@@ -154,6 +154,34 @@\n                (is (= v (jing/get b k nil))))))))))\n \n \n+#?(:cljd nil\n+   :clj\n+   (deftest non-portable-tag-decode-failure-is-dropped-not-fatal\n+     (testing\n+       \"a datagram outside dao.stream's portable domain is dropped on\n+        decode; the node keeps serving (D8: v2 decode throws where v1 did\n+        not, for a uuid/bigint/bigdec/uri/quoted/link tag)\"\n+       (with-cluster\n+         2\n+         (fn [[a b]]\n+           (let [port (:port (dht/self-peer (:net b)))\n+                 payload (.getBytes ^String\n+                          (transit/encode\n+                            {:op :ping, :rpc 0, :id (java.util.UUID/randomUUID)})\n+                                    \"UTF-8\")]\n+             (with-open [s (java.net.DatagramSocket.)]\n+               (.send s\n+                      (java.net.DatagramPacket.\n+                        payload\n+                        (alength payload)\n+                        (java.net.InetAddress/getByName \"127.0.0.1\")\n+                        (int port))))\n+             (Thread/sleep 100)\n+             (let [v {:bytes [43]}\n+                   k (jing/materialize! (:local a) v)]\n+               (is (= v (jing/get b k nil))))))))))\n+\n+\n #?(:cljd nil\n    :clj\n    (deftest rpc-failure-means-unreachable-not-thrown\n     1\t(ns dao.jing.dht.node\n     2\t  \"UDP Kademlia peer implementing dao.jing.dht/IDhtNet.\n     3\t\n     4\t  Wire format: one Transit-JSON message map per datagram. Requests carry\n     5\t  {:op ... :rpc n :from peer}; replies carry {:op :reply :rpc n :from peer\n     6\t  :value ...}. The wire ops are :ping, :find-node, :store-content, and\n     7\t  :fetch-content; there are no roots, no CAS records, and no deletes.\n     8\t  Request-response reliability is owned by the client as timeouts and\n     9\t  retries (design doc, Transport: chunk fetch is not gossip). Every\n    10\t  received :from is observed into the k-bucket table, so routing knowledge\n    11\t  accretes from traffic itself.\n    12\t\n    13\t  Limits, all named in docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:\n    14\t  - JVM only today (java.net.DatagramSocket); no browser/Node peer. The\n    15\t    file stays .cljc to match dao.stream.udp's convention and to leave\n    16\t    room for non-JVM transport branches; on other platforms it defines\n    17\t    nothing.\n    18\t  - One datagram per message: anything beyond max-datagram is refused on\n    19\t    send and dropped on reply, never torn. Segments that exceed the budget\n    20\t    stay local-only until DRDS fragmentation exists (store degrades to\n    21\t    best-effort, fetch times out).\n    22\t  - Peers are untrusted: incoming :store-content requests re-verify the\n    23\t    content address against the payload before writing. No address\n    24\t    validation or rate limiting yet (Operational reality, UDP\n    25\t    amplification).\"\n    26\t  #?(:clj (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n    27\t                    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    28\t                    [dao.jing.dht :as dht]\n    29\t                    [dao.jing.dht.kad :as kad]\n    30\t                    [dao.stream.transit :as transit]))\n    31\t  ;; :cljd nil must come FIRST: reader conditionals take the first\n    32\t  ;; matching branch, and the cljd host pass also matches :clj, so with\n    33\t  ;; :clj written first the import still reaches the Dart compiler.\n    34\t  ;; The :namespaces rule is disabled project-wide (see root .cljstyle)\n    35\t  ;; because it would otherwise reorder this to :clj-first on every\n    36\t  ;; `cljstyle fix`, silently re-breaking the guard.\n    37\t  #?(:cljd nil\n    38\t     :clj (:import (java.net DatagramPacket DatagramSocket InetAddress)\n    39\t                   (java.util.concurrent ConcurrentHashMap)\n    40\t                   (java.util.concurrent.atomic AtomicBoolean AtomicLong))))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t#?(:cljd nil\n    44\t   :clj\n    45\t   (def max-datagram\n    46\t     \"Conservative single-datagram payload budget. IPv6 guarantees only a\n    47\t     1280-byte path MTU; headers leave roughly this much (design doc,\n    48\t     Transport: 'MTU 1450 is optimistic').\"\n    49\t     1200))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t;; =============================================================================\n    53\t;; Codec\n    54\t;; =============================================================================\n    55\t\n    56\t#?(:cljd nil\n    57\t   :clj (defn- encode\n    58\t          ^bytes [msg]\n    59\t          (.getBytes ^String (transit/encode msg) \"UTF-8\")))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t#?(:cljd nil\n    63\t   :clj (defn- decode\n    64\t          [^DatagramPacket packet]\n    65\t          (transit/decode (String. (.getData packet)\n    66\t                                   (.getOffset packet)\n    67\t                                   (.getLength packet)\n    68\t                                   \"UTF-8\"))))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t#?(:cljd nil\n    72\t   :clj\n    73\t   (defn- send-datagram!\n    74\t     [^DatagramSocket socket ^bytes payload ^InetAddress addr port]\n    75\t     (when (> (alength payload) max-datagram)\n    76\t       (throw\n    77\t         (ex-info\n    78\t           \"payload exceeds the datagram budget; DRDS fragmentation is not implemented\"\n    79\t           {:size (alength payload), :max max-datagram})))\n    80\t     (.send socket\n    81\t            (DatagramPacket. payload (alength payload) addr (int port)))))\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t;; =============================================================================\n    85\t;; Request handling (the server half)\n    86\t;; =============================================================================\n    87\t\n    88\t#?(:cljd nil\n    89\t   :clj\n    90\t   (def ^:private missing\n    91\t     \"Internal not-found sentinel for served :fetch-content reads, never\n    92\t      exposed. An opaque per-host identity object, never a keyword: a\n    93\t      keyword sentinel could be confused with a genuinely stored payload,\n    94\t      and nil is a legal one.\"\n    95\t     (Object.)))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t#?(:cljd nil\n    99\t   :clj\n   100\t   (defn- handle\n   101\t     \"Serve one request against this node's local content store.\"\n   102\t     [local table msg]\n   103\t     (case (:op msg)\n   104\t       :ping {:pong true}\n   105\t       :find-node {:peers (kad/nearest @table (:target msg) kad/k)}\n   106\t       ;; peers are untrusted: the address must be the exact strict\n   107\t       ;; segment address for the payload, never a bare hash, a\n   108\t       ;; foreign namespace, or a mismatched value, and the local\n   109\t       ;; backend's verdict must be an explicit :inserted/:present\n   110\t       :store-content\n   111\t       (let [{:keys [address v]} msg]\n   112\t         (try\n   113\t           (if (and (jing/segment-address? address)\n   114\t                    (= (jing/segment-hash address) (jing/content-hash v)))\n   115\t             (let [result ((:put-content-fn local) address v)]\n   116\t               (if (#{:inserted :present} result) {:ok true} {:ok false}))\n   117\t             {:ok false})\n   118\t           (catch Exception _ {:ok false})))\n   119\t       ;; :found travels explicitly on both reads: values are opaque\n   120\t       ;; and nil is a legal one, so it cannot be inferred from :v\n   121\t       :fetch-content\n   122\t       (let [v (jing/get local (:address msg) missing)]\n   123\t         (if (identical? v missing) {:found false} {:found true, :v v}))\n   124\t       ;; no root or CAS op exists on this wire; unknown ops are\n   125\t       ;; thrown and answered as {:error ...} by the receiver\n   126\t       (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.dht.node: unknown op\" {:op (:op msg)})))))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t#?(:cljd nil\n   130\t   :clj\n   131\t   (defn- start-receiver!\n   132\t     \"One daemon thread per node: decodes datagrams, observes senders into\n   133\t      the routing table, delivers replies to pending requests, and serves\n   134\t      requests. Replies go to the datagram's source address, not the claimed\n   135\t      :from.\"\n   136\t     [^DatagramSocket socket local table self ^ConcurrentHashMap pending]\n   137\t     (doto\n   138\t       (Thread.\n   139\t         (fn []\n   140\t           (let [buf (byte-array 65536)\n   141\t                 packet (DatagramPacket. buf (alength buf))]\n   142\t             (while (not (.isClosed socket))\n   143\t               ;; three failure domains, contained separately so no\n   144\t               ;; single datagram or transient fault can kill the\n   145\t               ;; loop: the loop exits only when the socket closes\n   146\t               (when (try (.receive socket packet)\n   147\t                          true\n   148\t                          (catch Exception _\n   149\t                            ;; socket closed -> while exits; any\n   150\t                            ;; other receive fault: back off instead\n   151\t                            ;; of spinning hot. 10ms is not tuned,\n   152\t                            ;; only bounded: short enough to shrug\n   153\t                            ;; off a transient fault, long enough to\n   154\t                            ;; cap a persistent one at ~100\n   155\t                            ;; attempts/sec\n   156\t                            (when-not (.isClosed socket) (Thread/sleep 10))\n   157\t                            false))\n   158\t                 (let [msg (try (decode packet) (catch Exception _ nil))]\n   159\t                   (when (map? msg)\n   160\t                     (try (when-let [from (:from msg)]\n   161\t                            (when (not= (:id from) (:id self))\n   162\t                              (swap! table kad/observe (:id self) from)))\n   163\t                          (if (= :reply (:op msg))\n   164\t                            (when-let [p (.remove pending (:rpc msg))]\n   165\t                              (deliver p (:value msg)))\n   166\t                            (let [value (try (handle local table msg)\n   167\t                                             (catch Exception e\n   168\t                                               {:error (str (type e))}))\n   169\t                                  reply (encode {:op :reply,\n   170\t                                                 :rpc (:rpc msg),\n   171\t                                                 :from self,\n   172\t                                                 :value value})]\n   173\t                              ;; an oversized reply is dropped, not\n   174\t                              ;; torn; the requester times out and\n   175\t                              ;; treats this peer as not holding the\n   176\t                              ;; value\n   177\t                              (when (<= (alength reply) max-datagram)\n   178\t                                (.send socket\n   179\t                                       (DatagramPacket. reply\n   180\t                                                        (alength reply)\n   181\t                                                        (.getAddress packet)\n   182\t                                                        (.getPort packet))))))\n   183\t                          ;; a hostile message (e.g. malformed :from)\n   184\t                          ;; is dropped, never fatal\n   185\t                          (catch Exception _ nil)))))))))\n   186\t       (.setDaemon true)\n   187\t       (.start))))\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t;; =============================================================================\n   191\t;; Requests (the client half)\n   192\t;; =============================================================================\n   193\t\n   194\t#?(:cljd nil\n   195\t   :clj (defn- attempt!\n   196\t          [{:keys [^DatagramSocket socket ^ConcurrentHashMap pending\n   197\t                   ^AtomicLong rpc-counter peer]} to msg timeout-ms]\n   198\t          (let [rpc (.getAndIncrement rpc-counter)\n   199\t                p (promise)]\n   200\t            (.put pending rpc p)\n   201\t            (try (send-datagram! socket\n   202\t                                 (encode (assoc msg\n   203\t                                                :rpc rpc\n   204\t                                                :from peer))\n   205\t                                 (InetAddress/getByName (:host to))\n   206\t                                 (:port to))\n   207\t                 (deref p timeout-ms ::timeout)\n   208\t                 ;; an unresolvable host, a socket fault, or an oversized\n   209\t                 ;; payload is the same fact as silence: the peer is\n   210\t                 ;; unreachable, and the\n   211\t                 ;; IDhtNet contract wants nil, not a throw\n   212\t                 (catch Exception _ ::timeout)\n   213\t                 (finally (.remove pending rpc))))))\n   214\t\n   215\t\n   216\t#?(:cljd nil\n   217\t   :clj\n   218\t   (defn- request!\n   219\t     \"Request-response over fire-and-forget UDP: this client owns timeouts\n   220\t      and retries. Returns the reply value, or nil when the peer stays\n     1\t(ns dao.jing.dht.node-test\n     2\t  \"JVM integration tests for the UDP Kademlia node: real sockets on\n     3\t  localhost exchanging datagrams. The transport is JVM-only today (see\n     4\t  docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md, Transport), so every test is :clj-guarded;\n     5\t  the backend semantics themselves are covered cross-platform in\n     6\t  dao.jing.dht-test.\"\n     7\t  ;; :cljd nil must come FIRST (first matching branch wins and the cljd\n     8\t  ;; host pass also matches :clj): otherwise the host pass sees the\n     9\t  ;; deftests, registers a test namespace, and generates a Dart test\n    10\t  ;; entrypoint with no main. The :namespaces rule is disabled\n    11\t  ;; project-wide (see root .cljstyle) because it would otherwise flip\n    12\t  ;; this order back on every `cljstyle fix`.\n    13\t  #?(:cljd nil\n    14\t     :clj (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    15\t                    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    16\t                    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    17\t                    [dao.jing.dht :as dht]\n    18\t                    [dao.jing.dht.node :as node]\n    19\t                    [dao.stream.transit :as transit])))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t#?(:cljd nil\n    23\t   :clj\n    24\t   (defn- with-cluster\n    25\t     \"Run f with n DHT content stores over real UDP nodes on localhost, the\n    26\t      first node acting as the bootstrap peer for the rest. Closes\n    27\t      everything.\"\n    28\t     [n f]\n    29\t     (let [opts {:host \"127.0.0.1\", :timeout-ms 300, :tries 2}\n    30\t           head (node/create-content-dht-udp opts)\n    31\t           port (:port (dht/self-peer (:net head)))\n    32\t           tail (doall (repeatedly (dec n)\n    33\t                                   #(node/create-content-dht-udp\n    34\t                                      (assoc opts\n    35\t                                             :bootstrap [{:host \"127.0.0.1\",\n    36\t                                                          :port port}]))))\n    37\t           stores (into [head] tail)]\n    38\t       (try (f stores) (finally (run! jing/close! stores))))))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t#?(:cljd nil\n    42\t   :clj\n    43\t   (deftest udp-materialize-then-get-across-nodes\n    44\t     (testing\n    45\t       \"a payload materialized on one UDP node is fetched by another over the wire\"\n    46\t       (with-cluster 3\n    47\t         (fn [[a _ c]]\n    48\t           (let [v {:bytes [1 2 3]}\n    49\t                 k (jing/materialize! a v)]\n    50\t             (is (= v (jing/get c k nil)))))))))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t#?(:cljd nil\n    54\t   :clj\n    55\t   (deftest udp-forces-fetch-over-the-wire\n    56\t     (testing\n    57\t       \"a value materialized only into the local backend is fetched from the grid\"\n    58\t       (with-cluster 2\n    59\t         (fn [[a b]]\n    60\t           (let [v {:bytes [9]}\n    61\t                 k (jing/materialize! (:local a) v)]\n    62\t             (is (= v (jing/get b k ::none)))))))))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t#?(:cljd nil\n    66\t   :clj (deftest udp-stored-nil-forces-fetch\n    67\t          (testing \"nil is a legal stored payload and survives the wire fetch\"\n    68\t            (with-cluster 2\n    69\t              (fn [[a b]]\n    70\t                (let [k (jing/materialize! (:local a) nil)]\n    71\t                  (is (= nil (jing/get b k ::none)))))))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t#?(:cljd nil\n    75\t   :clj\n    76\t   (deftest store-handler-enforces-address-and-hash\n    77\t     (testing\n    78\t       \"an incoming :store-content must present the exact strict segment address\"\n    79\t       (let [handle (deref #'node/handle)\n    80\t             local (mem/create-content-mem)\n    81\t             table (atom {})\n    82\t             v {:bytes [1]}\n    83\t             hash (jing/content-hash v)\n    84\t             k (jing/segment-key v)]\n    85\t         (is (true? (:ok (handle local\n    86\t                                 table\n    87\t                                 {:op :store-content, :address k, :v v}))))\n    88\t         (is (false? (:ok (handle local\n    89\t                                  table\n    90\t                                  {:op :store-content, :address hash, :v v})))\n    91\t             \"a bare hash string is not a content address\")\n    92\t         (is (false? (:ok (handle local\n    93\t                                  table\n    94\t                                  {:op :store-content,\n    95\t                                   :address (keyword \"root\" hash),\n    96\t                                   :v v})))\n    97\t             \"a :root key cannot be planted via :store-content\")\n    98\t         (is (false? (:ok (handle local\n    99\t                                  table\n   100\t                                  {:op :store-content,\n   101\t                                   :address (jing/segment-key {:bytes [2]}),\n   102\t                                   :v v})))\n   103\t             \"an address that does not hash to the payload is refused\")\n   104\t         (is (= v (jing/get local k ::miss))\n   105\t             \"only the exact-address write was stored\")\n   106\t         (is (= ::miss ((:get-content-fn local) hash ::miss)))\n   107\t         (is (= ::miss\n   108\t                ((:get-content-fn local) (keyword \"root\" hash) ::miss)))\n   109\t         (is (= ::miss\n   110\t                (jing/get local (jing/segment-key {:bytes [2]}) ::miss)))))))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t#?(:cljd nil\n   114\t   :clj (deftest root-ops-are-unsupported\n   115\t          (testing \"the wire knows no root or CAS ops\"\n   116\t            (let [handle (deref #'node/handle)\n   117\t                  local (mem/create-content-mem)]\n   118\t              (is (thrown? Exception\n   119\t                    (handle local {} {:op :root-get, :k :root/head})))\n   120\t              (is (thrown? Exception\n   121\t                    (handle local\n   122\t                            {}\n   123\t                            {:op :root-cas,\n   124\t                             :k :root/head,\n   125\t                             :expected 0,\n   126\t                             :v {:p \"x\"}})))))))\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\t#?(:cljd nil\n   130\t   :clj\n   131\t   (deftest hostile-datagram-does-not-kill-the-receiver\n   132\t     (testing\n   133\t       \"a datagram with a malformed :from is dropped; the node keeps serving\"\n   134\t       (with-cluster\n   135\t         2\n   136\t         (fn [[a b]]\n   137\t           (let [port (:port (dht/self-peer (:net b)))\n   138\t                 payload (.getBytes ^String\n   139\t                          (transit/encode\n   140\t                            {:op :ping, :rpc 0, :from {:id 42}})\n   141\t                                    \"UTF-8\")]\n   142\t             (with-open [s (java.net.DatagramSocket.)]\n   143\t               (.send s\n   144\t                      (java.net.DatagramPacket.\n   145\t                        payload\n   146\t                        (alength payload)\n   147\t                        (java.net.InetAddress/getByName \"127.0.0.1\")\n   148\t                        (int port))))\n   149\t             (Thread/sleep 100)\n   150\t             ;; b's receiver must survive to deliver the reply to the\n   151\t             ;; forced fetch, whose value never replicated off a\n   152\t             (let [v {:bytes [42]}\n   153\t                   k (jing/materialize! (:local a) v)]\n   154\t               (is (= v (jing/get b k nil))))))))))\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\t#?(:cljd nil\n   158\t   :clj\n   159\t   (deftest non-portable-tag-decode-failure-is-dropped-not-fatal\n   160\t     (testing\n   161\t       \"a datagram outside dao.stream's portable domain is dropped on\n   162\t        decode; the node keeps serving (D8: v2 decode throws where v1 did\n   163\t        not, for a uuid/bigint/bigdec/uri/quoted/link tag)\"\n   164\t       (with-cluster\n   165\t         2\n   166\t         (fn [[a b]]\n   167\t           (let [port (:port (dht/self-peer (:net b)))\n   168\t                 payload (.getBytes ^String\n   169\t                          (transit/encode\n   170\t                            {:op :ping, :rpc 0, :id (java.util.UUID/randomUUID)})\n   171\t                                    \"UTF-8\")]\n   172\t             (with-open [s (java.net.DatagramSocket.)]\n   173\t               (.send s\n   174\t                      (java.net.DatagramPacket.\n   175\t                        payload\n   176\t                        (alength payload)\n   177\t                        (java.net.InetAddress/getByName \"127.0.0.1\")\n   178\t                        (int port))))\n   179\t             (Thread/sleep 100)\n   180\t             (let [v {:bytes [43]}\n   181\t                   k (jing/materialize! (:local a) v)]\n   182\t               (is (= v (jing/get b k nil))))))))))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t#?(:cljd nil\n   186\t   :clj\n   187\t   (deftest rpc-failure-means-unreachable-not-thrown\n   188\t     (testing\n   189\t       \"a host that cannot be resolved or reached yields nil/false per the\n   190\t       IDhtNet contract, never an exception\"\n   191\t       (let [net (node/create-node\n   192\t                   {:host \"127.0.0.1\", :timeout-ms 100, :tries 1})\n   193\t             bad {:id (dht/node-id \"bad\" 1),\n   194\t                  :host \"invalid host name with spaces\",\n   195\t                  :port 1}]\n   196\t         (try (is (nil? (dht/fetch-content net bad :segment/abc)))\n   197\t              (is (nil? (dht/find-closer net bad (dht/node-id \"t\" 0))))\n   198\t              (is (false?\n   199\t                    (dht/store-content! net bad :segment/abc {:bytes [1]})))\n   200\t              (finally (dht/close-net! net)))))))\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\t#?(:cljd nil\n   204\t   :clj\n   205\t   (deftest udp-packet-size-variation\n   206\t     (testing\n   207\t       \"packets of varying sizes can be received sequentially without truncation\"\n   208\t       (with-cluster 2\n   209\t         (fn [[a b]]\n   210\t           (let [v-small {:bytes [1]}\n   211\t                 k-small (jing/materialize! (:local a) v-small)\n   212\t                 v-large {:bytes (vec (repeat 400 2))}\n   213\t                 k-large (jing/materialize! (:local a) v-large)]\n   214\t             ;; 1. Small forced fetch (sets receiver packet\n   215\t             ;; length to small)\n   216\t             (is (= v-small (jing/get b k-small nil)))\n   217\t             ;; 2. Large forced fetch (should not be\n   218\t             ;; truncated)\n   219\t             (is (= v-large (jing/get b k-large nil)))))))))\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t#?(:cljd nil\n   223\t   :clj\n   224\t   (deftest udp-oversized-segment-stays-local\n   225\t     (testing\n   226\t       \"payloads beyond the datagram budget degrade to local-only until DRDS exists\"\n   227\t       (with-cluster\n   228\t         2\n   229\t         (fn [[a b]]\n   230\t           (let [v {:bytes (apply str (repeat 3000 \"x\"))}\n   231\t                 k (jing/materialize! a v)]\n   232\t             (is (= v (jing/get a k nil))\n   233\t                 \"the local write succeeds; replication is best-effort\")\n   234\t             (is (= ::none (jing/get b k ::none))\n   235\t                 \"the payload cannot cross the wire yet\")))))))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t#?(:cljd nil\n   239\t   :clj (deftest udp-close-is-idempotent\n   240\t          (with-cluster 1\n   241\t            (fn [[a]]\n   242\t              (is (nil? (jing/close! a)))\n   243\t              (is (nil? (jing/close! a))\n   244\t                  \"closing twice is safe\")))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
