{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/clj/dao/stream/transit.clj | sed -n '1,180p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md | sed -n '560,610p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md | sed -n '1024,1042p'; nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.md | sed -n '786,824p'; rg -n \\\"dao\\\\.stream(?:\\\\.transit)?\\\" src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc; rg -n \\\"dao\\\\.stream\\\\.transit\\\" src/clj/dao/jing src/cljc/dao/jing src/cljs/dao/jing test/dao/jing 2>/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.transit\n     2\t  \"Transit JSON support for stream link messages.\n     3\t\n     4\t   This namespace provides the `:json` reader and writer shape used by the\n     5\t   datom.world stream layer. It delegates to `cognitect.transit` on the JVM,\n     6\t   and mirrors the CLJD implementation so callers can use the same API on all\n     7\t   supported platforms.\"\n     8\t  (:refer-clojure :exclude [read bigint bigdec])\n     9\t  (:require\n    10\t    [cognitect.transit :as transit])\n    11\t  (:import\n    12\t    (java.io\n    13\t      ByteArrayInputStream\n    14\t      ByteArrayOutputStream)))\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\t(defn reader\n    18\t  \"Construct a Transit reader for `:json`.\"\n    19\t  ([source kind]\n    20\t   (reader source kind nil))\n    21\t  ([source kind opts]\n    22\t   (transit/reader source kind opts)))\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\t(defn writer\n    26\t  \"Construct a Transit writer for `:json`.\"\n    27\t  ([sink kind]\n    28\t   (writer sink kind nil))\n    29\t  ([sink kind opts]\n    30\t   (transit/writer sink kind opts)))\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(defn read\n    34\t  \"Decode transit JSON from a reader and source string.\"\n    35\t  ([r]\n    36\t   (transit/read r))\n    37\t  ([r source]\n    38\t   (transit/read r)))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defn write\n    42\t  \"Encode a value into transit JSON and append it to the writer sink.\"\n    43\t  [w v]\n    44\t  (transit/write w v))\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn read-handler\n    48\t  \"Construct a transit read handler.\"\n    49\t  [from-rep]\n    50\t  (transit/read-handler from-rep))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn write-handler\n    54\t  \"Construct a transit write handler.\"\n    55\t  ([tag-fn rep-fn]\n    56\t   (transit/write-handler tag-fn rep-fn))\n    57\t  ([tag-fn rep-fn str-rep-fn]\n    58\t   (transit/write-handler tag-fn rep-fn str-rep-fn)))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn tagged-value\n    62\t  \"Construct a tagged transit value.\"\n    63\t  [tag rep]\n    64\t  (transit/tagged-value tag rep))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn integer\n    68\t  \"Construct a transit integer value.\"\n    69\t  [n]\n    70\t  n)\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(defn bigint\n    74\t  \"Construct a transit big integer value.\"\n    75\t  [n]\n    76\t  (clojure.core/bigint n))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defn bigdec\n    80\t  \"Construct a transit big decimal value.\"\n    81\t  [s]\n    82\t  (clojure.core/bigdec s))\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t(defn uri\n    86\t  \"Construct a transit URI value.\"\n    87\t  [s]\n    88\t  (java.net.URI. (str s)))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn uuid\n    92\t  \"Construct a transit UUID value.\"\n    93\t  [s]\n    94\t  (java.util.UUID/fromString (str s)))\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t(defn binary\n    98\t  \"Construct a transit binary value.\"\n    99\t  [s]\n   100\t  (cond\n   101\t    (string? s) (.decode (java.util.Base64/getDecoder) s)\n   102\t    :else s))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(defn quoted\n   106\t  \"Construct a quoted transit value.\"\n   107\t  [x]\n   108\t  (transit/tagged-value \"'\" x))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(defn link\n   112\t  \"Construct a transit link value.\"\n   113\t  [x]\n   114\t  (transit/tagged-value \"link\" x))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(defn write-meta\n   118\t  \"Wrap metadata-bearing values so the writer can emit `~#with-meta`.\"\n   119\t  [x]\n   120\t  (transit/write-meta x))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn encode\n   124\t  \"Encode a value to Transit JSON text.\"\n   125\t  [msg]\n   126\t  (let [out (ByteArrayOutputStream.)]\n   127\t    (write (writer out :json) msg)\n   128\t    (.toString out \"UTF-8\")))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn decode\n   132\t  \"Decode Transit JSON text into a value.\"\n   133\t  [s]\n   134\t  (let [in (ByteArrayInputStream. (.getBytes s \"UTF-8\"))]\n   135\t    (read (reader in :json))))\n   560\tsocket, as `parse-url` reports them.\n   561\t\n   562\tThe function is **public**, so its portable test needs no `#'` seam; it is\n   563\t`dao.jing.remote`'s own twenty lines, not a require of\n   564\t`yin.repl.connect`: `dao.*` does not depend on `yin.*`, and `parse-url`\n   565\tcarries REPL rules (`daostream:` prefix, `/repl` default) that do not belong\n   566\there. Lifting the generic part into `dao.stream.ws` beside\n   567\t`canonical-path?` would serve both and is owed nowhere (§8).\n   568\t\n   569\t### D8 — `dao.jing.dht.node` is a separate plan, and its work is on the decode side\n   570\t\n   571\tTwo namespaces under `dao.jing` are listed together in `dao.stream.md` because\n   572\tof their parent, not their transport. `dht.node` is a UDP peer with no\n   573\tDaoStream in it; its only v1 dependency is `dao.stream.transit`'s codec\n   574\t(correction 8), so splitting is right and this plan makes **no edit under\n   575\t`dao/jing/dht`**.\n   576\t\n   577\tr1 called the second plan \"a require swap\". It is not. v1 `dao.stream.transit`\n   578\tdelegates straight to cognitect; `dao.stream.transit` runs\n   579\t`ensure-portable!` on **both** `encode` and `decode` (`v2/transit.cljc:100,\n   580\t121`), and the portable domain excludes the tagged values cognitect decodes\n   581\thappily — uuid, bigint, bigdec, uri, quoted, link. The outbound direction is\n   582\tthe easy check (every map `dht.node` builds is keywords, strings, safe\n   583\tintegers and content payloads). **The inbound direction is the work**: a\n   584\tdatagram from any peer carrying one of those tags would newly throw inside\n   585\t`decode`, in the receive path, and the plan that swaps the require has to\n   586\tdecide what the node does with a datagram it cannot decode — drop it as v1\n   587\tdrops an oversize one, most likely — and pin that with a hostile-datagram\n   588\ttest. That is a small plan, but it is a plan about a wire, not a require.\n   589\t\n   590\t---\n   591\t\n   592\t## 4. Phases 0 and 1\n   593\t\n   594\t### 4.0 Phase 0 — repair the JVM send seam — **DONE, `3228d0e`**\n   595\t\n   596\tCommitted 2026-09-10 ahead of the migration, on its own, as this section\n   597\tplanned. What follows describes **what shipped**, not what was drafted: three\n   598\treview rounds changed it in two respects, and a plan that misdescribes the\n   599\tcommit it produced is worse than no plan. The divergences are marked.\n   600\t\n   601\t`src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj`, and a new\n   602\t`test/dao/stream/ws/jvm_test.clj`. No public signature changed and no\n   603\tconsumer moved.\n   604\t\n   605\t**Built**\n   606\t\n   607\t- The client socket view is extracted from `connect!` into a public\n   608\t  `client-socket [connection adapter]` returning the `{:send! :close!}` map,\n   609\t  so it can be driven against a controlled `java.net.http.WebSocket` without\n   610\t  a network. `connect!` calls it.\n  1024\t---\n  1025\t\n  1026\t## 8. Boundary — built here, and what is left owing by namespace\n  1027\t\n  1028\tBuilt here: Phase 0's repair of `dao.stream.ws.jvm` (done);\n  1029\t`dao.jing.remote` on v2 (both halves), its tests, the two fixtures that pair\n  1030\tthem, four documents.\n  1031\t\n  1032\t| owed | by | where it is recorded |\n  1033\t|---|---|---|\n  1034\t| **The establishment-cancel gap in the JVM edge**: `close!` before `onOpen` records a `:close-request` and does not cancel or abort the pending establishment, so a disconnect while connecting leaves the JDK connection held. Live today for `yin.repl`'s `(disconnect)` during `:connecting`; live for `dao.jing.remote` on a connect timeout against a stalled peer (N2). What the repair needs to know is in §9 | `dao.stream.ws.jvm` — transport work, on its own ticket, with `yin.repl` as its first consumer; **not** `dao.jing.remote`, which has no handle to reach it | `dao.stream.ws.md` *Deferred*, written in Phase 2's doc step (§5.4) |\n  1035\t| `dao.jing.dht.node` and `node_test` off `dao.stream.transit`, including the inbound decode policy for non-portable datagrams | its own plan (D8) | `dao.stream.md`'s consumer list keeps the DHT node |\n  1036\t| a non-blocking remote handle — the stepped client with multi-id dispatch, and the consumer change it forces on B-tree hydration | `dao.data.btree.md` §5.4 / `dao.jing.md` *Open items* | §9 moves Decision 3's sketch there |\n  1037\t| deletion of `dao.stream.rpc.*`, `dao.stream.ws`, `dao.stream.transit`, v1 `yin.repl` | the v1 deletion, per `dao.stream.md` | already recorded there |\n  1038\t| whether the Dart edge's close-before-connect (`dart.cljd:121-137`, a stored request applied on connect) shares the gap — it cancels nothing either, though Dart's `WebSocket.connect` future is its own object | nobody; noted for the owner beside the JVM row | not this plan's host; the JVM is the only host `dao.jing.remote` runs on |\n  1039\t| a generic URL→descriptor parser shared with `yin.repl.connect` | nobody | optional; two private parsers is the cost |\n  1040\t| `dao.stream.ws.jvm/listen!` deposits `:yin.repl.endpoint/*` codes from a `dao.*` namespace | nobody; noted for the owner | a naming leak, harmless to this plan; Phase 0 did not touch `listen!` |\n  1041\t| `yin.repl.implementation-plan.md:728` and `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:122` say `dao.stream.rpc.*` \"keeps serving `dao.jing.remote`\" | the owner — both describe their own slice's boundary at the time | left as written; they become historical the moment Phase 2 lands |\n  1042\t\n   786\t  be the same defect as asking whether it is closed: the answer is\n   787\t  configuration the composition already holds, and reading it back at runtime\n   788\t  invites code that branches on what it should have been wired with.\n   789\t\n   790\t## The v2 namespace is transient\n   791\t\n   792\t`dao.stream` exists to protect a working system while its consumers move,\n   793\tnot to live forever. When the last consumer has migrated under its own plan\n   794\tand legacy `dao.stream` is deleted, **`dao.stream` is renamed to\n   795\t`dao.stream`** — decided, not left open. An undecided coexistence of both\n   796\tnamespaces is a defect of the migration, not a steady state.\n   797\t\n   798\tThis is recorded here because the plan that carried it,\n   799\t`dao.stream.implementation-plan.md`, was consumed when its phases\n   800\tcompleted; the decision it left open outlived it, and a transient plan is\n   801\tsafe to delete only once nothing in it is still owed.\n   802\t\n   803\tThe remaining v1 consumers, each migrating under its own plan:\n   804\t`yin.io`'s file transports with `dao.gui.event` and\n   805\t`dao.postgraphics.terminal`, `dao.runtime` (gated on the v1 VM's deletion),\n   806\t`agent.tools`, and the demo and server surfaces. The v1 VM lineage is deleted\n   807\trather than migrated, under `yin.vm-consumers.implementation-plan.md`,\n   808\tbecause a v2 twin already exists for every one of its consumers. So are the v1\n   809\ttransports themselves — `dao.stream.{apply, file, file-input-stream,\n   810\tfile-output-stream, http, link, ringbuffer, udp, ws}` and `dao.stream.rpc.*`,\n   811\twith their ClojureDart siblings: they are v1's own implementation, not\n   812\tconsumers of it, and they go when it does rather than acquiring v2 twins one\n   813\tby one.\n   814\t\n   815\t`dao.space` is done: `query`, `index` and `transactor` require `dao.stream`,\n   816\tand `schema` and `transact` require no stream namespace at all.\ntest/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc:19:                    [dao.stream.transit :as transit])))\ntest/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc:161:       \"a datagram outside dao.stream's portable domain is dropped on\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc:15:    file stays .cljc to match dao.stream.udp's convention and to leave\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc:30:                    [dao.stream.transit :as transit]))\ntest/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc:19:                    [dao.stream.transit :as transit])))\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
