{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"## Findings\n\n- **[P1] The migration leaves `node_test` dependent on v1.** [node_test.cljc:19](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc:19) still requires `dao.stream.transit`. This contradicts D8’s explicit requirement that both `dao.jing.dht.node` and `node_test` move off that namespace, and would break this test when v1 is deleted. Consequently, removing the DHT node from the remaining-consumers list at [dao.stream.md:803](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:803) is premature. Generate the hostile datagram directly with `cognitect.transit` or a local test helper instead.\n\n- **[P2] The new test proves liveness, but not that the UUID datagram was rejected.** [node_test.cljc:159](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc:159) would also pass if the node decoded and handled the otherwise-valid `:ping`; it only checks that a later fetch succeeds. Assert that the sender receives no ping reply, or separately assert that the constructed packet throws through the node’s decoder, before checking receiver liveness.\n\nThe production containment itself is correct: [node.cljc:158](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc:158) catches the `ExceptionInfo` thrown by `ensure-portable!`, returns `nil`, and bypasses `map?` and all handling. UUID is a faithful v1-accepted/v2-rejected tagged value. No other production v1 dependency remains in `dao.jing.dht.node`.\n\n**Verdict:** Request changes; low implementation risk. I did not rerun the supplied tests."}}
